sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch05-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch05-03--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch05-03--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch05-03: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.89" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.89"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/computation" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.88"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The rule, the initial row, and the claimed circular outline are concrete, and the evolution is an exact finite cellular automaton. Public simulators can run it for far more than the 400 steps in the figure and report a circularity statistic with an obvious confirming or refuting range. Grid anisotropy is precisely what the measurement is designed to detect, so the test discriminates the claim from a merely blob-like growth." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Run the stated eight-neighbor rule (black only with exactly three black neighbors, with the published survival and death cases) from a short row of black cells, and measure circularity and the quadrupolar Fourier component of the boundary against a circle of radius about 0.37t. Circularity staying near 1 at large t confirms the approximation; a persistent square or diamond anisotropy would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "On a square lattice a perfect circle is impossible, so 'closely approximate' needs a numeric tolerance such as circularity or radial error.", "Very large t is cheap but not infinite; a late drift away from circularity would still count against the claim." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch05-03--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch05-03--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch05-03--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch05-03 by Grok 4.7: 0.9" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.9"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch05-03--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch05-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch05-03--grok--operationalizability> .
